    a name or an address, then an optional colon and port. A name is letters,
    digits, hyphens, dots and underscores; an IPv6 address goes in square
    brackets. That is narrower than RFC 3986 allows, on purpose: nothing a
    real host is called needs more, and what is left out (@ , / ? # % and
    spaces) is what gets a URL built from this value to point somewhere else.
    Empty text is allowed, as a request without an authority sends it.
